# The assessment of AGT-EXEC-001 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-EXEC-001: "Agent capabilities shall be partitioned into read, propose, preview,
# mutate, execute, approve, and publish classes with separate authorization and audit
# requirements."
#
# The prior audit (P13-TRACE-AGT-EXEC-AUDIT) left this Unassessed, finding no legitimate
# site. Re-checked directly: `AuthorityClass` (`nomos-contracts`) is a real, deliberately
# designed enum partitioning agent capability into exactly the seven classes this
# requirement names -- Read, Propose, Preview, Mutate, Execute, Approve, Publish, verbatim
# -- and `Requires_Explicit_Grant` gives a real, if binary, per-class authorization
# distinction. It was simply never cited before now.
#
# But no operation anywhere in the live workspace actually carries or is checked against
# `AuthorityClass` -- zero consumers outside its own declaring module -- and no
# audit-requirement concept of any kind exists tied to authority. `Claim` (`nomos-ledger`,
# the concrete shape an agent's run already takes here, per AGT-EXEC-002's own committed
# assessment) carries who holds an item and when the lease lapses, nothing about which class
# the held work exercises. `VerificationRecord` is the nearest real audit-shaped artifact
# anywhere (argv, exit code, output tail, timestamp, gate, revision), but it is scoped to one
# ledger item's finish-predicate verification, never keyed by `AuthorityClass`, and has no
# counterpart for Propose/Approve/Publish, which have no implemented operation at all.
# `nomos_corrections::ValidatedPlan::Commit` independently reinvents a state machine
# (Stage -> Validate -> Commit -> Rollback) that structurally parallels `MutationClass`
# (Preview -> Validate -> Apply -> Rollback), and OD-CORRECTIONS-002 just added `Evidence` to
# it -- but `Commit` still takes no `AuthorityClass` and records nothing an auditor could call
# a per-capability-class trail; that record's own "What This Does Not Do" section states
# directly it "does not build AGT-EXEC-001's capability-class partitioning or
# authorization/audit model," corroborating this finding independently. So "partitioned into
# classes" is met at the type level while "separate authorization and audit requirements" has
# no operational reality.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/contracts/nomos-contracts/src/authority/class.rs#AuthorityClass
site: crates/contracts/nomos-contracts/src/authority/class.rs#Requires_Explicit_Grant
site: crates/contracts/nomos-contracts/src/authority/mutation_class.rs#MutationClass
gap: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/claim.rs#Claim
gap: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/verification/record.rs#VerificationRecord
gap: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/validated.rs#Commit
